From c7b5f6efe165ec4687a8e22ad0efd699469e056c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:52:41 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] ARM64: Pass variadic HFAs as plain composites on
 Windows

The Windows ARM64 ABI uses no FP/SIMD registers for variadic functions
and treats HFAs/HVAs like any other composite: arguments are laid out
on an imaginary stack whose first 64 bytes are x0-x7.  ffi_call and the
closure handler instead gave each HFA member its own X register (via
the 16-byte-stride extend/compress helpers), did not pass HFAs larger
than 16 bytes by reference, and never split a composite between x7 and
the stack.  A variadic call with an HFA argument crashed.

Treat FP values and HFAs/HVAs in FFI_WIN64 variadic calls as ordinary
composites, split them between the last X registers and the stack when
needed, and reserve the by-reference pointer slot for large HFAs.

Add libffi.call/va_hfa.c, which calls and implements a variadic
function with float and double HFAs of every size after 0-7 integer
arguments.
